  "scope": "Private Vulkan/JWM/X11 real late-foreground close intent, embedded Vim9, explicit final-tab confirmation and sampled full family matrix. The late job is launched by native shell input and takes actual kernel PTY foreground; it is not an ordinary shell fg UX test. No synthetic residence/native proof is injected.",
  "implemented": [
    "Ember separates an already-started withdrawal from GUI close permission: new terminal work pauses exit until a fresh close request, without cancelling or fabricating old-token proof.",
    "Frost rechecks fresh kernel PTY foreground across owned interactive panes during guarded window withdrawal. New work pauses both automatic exit and the blocking closing overlay, preserving native input; fresh window close explicitly rearms.",
    "The final pane retains its own explicit process-confirmation/completion path; Frost final-session exit clears the whole-window guard instead of blocking an already authorized close."
  ],
